This inlines the base-class lookup: it calls `GetField(254)` directly and reads index 0 of the main field. That skips one level of call and the subfield-mode check for a field that has no subfields.

It returns the same value as before only if `Mesg::GetFieldUINT16Value` does what I recalled; I did not check its source:
- it returns `FIT_UINT16_INVALID` when the field is absent;
- otherwise it returns `field->GetUINT16Value(0, FIT_SUBFIELD_INDEX_MAIN_FIELD)`.

It also assumes `const Field* GetField(FIT_UINT8) const` is accessible from this class. If either assumption is wrong, this rewrite is not safe.

```cpp
    FIT_MESSAGE_INDEX GetMessageIndex(void) const
    {
        const Field* field = GetField(254);
        if (field == FIT_NULL)
            return FIT_UINT16_INVALID;
        return field->GetUINT16Value(0, FIT_SUBFIELD_INDEX_MAIN_FIELD);
    }
```